# [[ project_name ]]

[[ project_description ]]

ESP32 C++ firmware with a hexagonal (ports & adapters) architecture, optimised for agentic coding with Claude Code.

## Quick start

```bash
uv sync                       # one-time: install Python tooling
pio test -e native            # fast host-side tests (GoogleTest)
pio run  -e esp32s3           # build target firmware
pio run  -e esp32s3 -t upload # flash via built-in USB-JTAG
pio device monitor -e esp32s3 # serial console
pio test -e test_esp32s3      # on-chip Unity tests (slow)
[% if enable_hil %]
uv run pytest -m hil          # HIL bench tests (scope + PPK2)
[% endif %]
```

## Where things live

- `components/core/` — pure logic. No hardware includes. Compiles on your laptop.
- `components/adapters_esp32/` — real ESP-IDF implementations.
- `components/adapters_fake/` — fakes for native tests.
- `components/drivers/` — device drivers (talk to ports, not hardware).
- `main/main.cpp` — composition root (wires adapters to core).
- `tools/sim/` — optional Python device simulation.
[% if enable_hil %]
- `tools/hil/` — hardware-in-the-loop bench (Siglent SDS1104X-E + Nordic PPK2).
[% endif %]

